<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency Check suppressions.

  RULES FOR THIS FILE — read before adding an entry:

  1. A suppression is a statement that a REPORTED vulnerability does not apply
     to this project. It is not a way to make a red build green. If the CVE
     applies, upgrade the dependency instead.

  2. Every entry MUST carry:
       - the CVE id,
       - a <notes> explaining WHY it does not apply here (which code path is
         absent, which feature is not enabled),
       - an expiry date in the notes, no more than 90 days out.

  3. An undated suppression is a permanently disabled gate. Re-review on expiry;
     if the CVE still has no fix, re-date it deliberately rather than leaving it
     open forever.

  4. NEVER raise failBuildOnCVSS in pom.xml to clear a finding. That disables
     the gate for every dependency, forever, invisibly. This file at least makes
     each exemption reviewable in a diff.

  Currently empty: no exemptions are in force. Remediation so far has been by
  upgrading spring-boot-starter-parent, which is always the preferred fix
  because it moves the whole managed dependency set at once.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
</suppressions>
